  "reply": "Now I have everything I need. Let me implement the fix:All 26 tests pass (10 accept + 16 reject). \n\n**What changed in `src/duration.ts`:** Replaced the stub that only matched `NNms` with a full parser that:\n- Strips optional leading/trailing whitespace and between components\n- Matches one or more components with `/^(\\d+)(h|ms|s|m)/` (alternation orders `ms` before `m` to avoid partial matches)\n- Enforces strictly descending unit order `h → m → s → ms`, rejecting duplicates and out-of-order sequences\n- Rejects signs, decimals, unknown units, and bare integers since the regex only matches raw `\\d+` followed by a valid unit\n- Guards against overflow in two stages: `value > maxComp[unit]` (single component × multiplier would exceed `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`) and `total > MAX − contrib` (cumulative sum would exceed `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`)\n- Throws `RangeError` on empty input, whitespace-only input, and all other invalid inputs",
